LICENSING STATUS AND SCOPE

This repository has mixed provenance. This file is a licensing-status notice,
not a repository-wide grant under MIT, Apache-2.0, or any other software license.

1. Upstream-derived software and documentation

The trainer and other inherited files originate from
https://github.com/IAmIronMan42/MiniMax-H3-FineTuning
at upstream commit 74d535b2cae5cd56f9565059e6f2b6c9ddb39df4.
No declared software license was found in that source tree. Its README links
the model-weight license, not a separate license for this third-party trainer.
This project does not grant rights in, or relicense, the upstream authors'
material. Modified inherited files retain that distinction; adding new code
to a file does not license the entire file. See NOTICE for the provenance map.

2. Separable new optimization, testing, and documentation contributions

The new contributions identified in NOTICE are distinct from inherited
material. No additional software or documentation license grant is made by
this notice for those contributions. In particular, they are not silently
placed under MIT or Apache-2.0, and their existence does not supply a license
for upstream-derived code. Any future separate license must identify its
covered contributions and come from the appropriate rights holders.

3. Model materials and model derivatives

MiniMax H3 model materials, including released weights, and model derivatives
are governed by the applicable MiniMax H3 Community License Agreement:
https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3/blob/main/LICENSE
That agreement includes territory, use, and redistribution conditions. It is
not replaced by this file and is not asserted here as a blanket software
license for the upstream third-party fine-tuning repository. Fine-tuned model
weights and LoRA checkpoints must be considered separately from software/docs.
The Git source tree contains no model-weight checkpoint or training cache.
A code/documentation notice does not authorize distribution of model artifacts.

4. Dependencies and example assets

External libraries and separately sourced assets retain their own terms.
Example-image provenance and notices remain in examples/public_assets/SOURCES.md.
This file grants no rights in third-party dependencies or assets.

See NOTICE and docs/licensing-provenance.json for scope and primary sources.
